# Everything the image does not need, kept out of the build context so it is neither uploaded to the
# daemon nor able to end up in a layer.
#
# `appsettings.Development.json` is the one that matters. It is gitignored, so it exists only on a
# developer's machine — and a developer's machine is exactly where a real connection string lives.
# Without this line, `COPY src/ src/` would bake it into the image.

**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/*.user

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/

.git/
.github/
.githooks/

web/
docs/
infra/
tests/

**/node_modules/
**/.env
**/.env.*

docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
